From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: rockchip: clear failed clock before bulk cleanup

When of_clk_get() fails, the clock array retains its error pointer.
The error path passes the whole array to clk_bulk_put(), which tolerates
NULL entries but warns when clk_put() receives an error pointer.

Clear the failed entry before releasing the clocks acquired so far.
The remaining entries are already zeroed by devm_kcalloc(). This avoids
tainting the kernel on an ordinary deferred probe.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -851,6 +851,7 @@
 		pd->clks[i].clk = of_clk_get(node, i);
 		if (IS_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk)) {
 			error = PTR_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk);
+			pd->clks[i].clk = NULL;
 			dev_err(pmu->dev,
 				"%pOFn: failed to get clk at index %d: %d\n",
 				node, i, error);
